          "",
          "### References without a DOI\n",
          "These references have no DOI, so they could not be checked here, and they also cannot be checked by the other reference modules (retraction, PubPeer, and replication checks all rely on the DOI). We searched CrossRef for a matching DOI; where a confident match was found it is suggested below. We recommend adding a DOI to every reference that has one: it lets these checks run and makes each cited work easier to find and verify.\n",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Reference = c(\"DeBruine, Lisa. 2025. Faux: Simulation for Factorial Designs. Zenodo. https: //doi.org/10.5281/10.5281/zenodo.2669586.\", \n\"Smith, F. 2021. \\\"Human Error Is a Symptom of a Poor Design.\\\" Journal of Journals. https://doi.org/10.0000/0123456789.\"\n), \"Suggested DOI\" = c(\"\", \"\")), row.names = c(NA, -2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, c(0.7, 0.3), 5, FALSE)\n```\n"
